Instructions here: https://community.platformio.org/t/how-to-use-stm32wl55jc-under-stm32cube-framework/32926. Make sure to modify the platform.io `platform.json` file located at `~/.platformio/platforms/ststm32/platform.json` to include:

```
    "framework-stm32cubewl": {
      "type": "framework",
      "optional": true,
      "owner": "platformio",
      "version": "symlink://C:/path/to/here/STM32CubeWL"
    },
```

underneath:
```
    "framework-zephyr": {
    "type": "framework",
```

Also modify `nucleo_wl55jc.json` at `~/.platformio/platforms/ststm32/boards/nucleo_wl55jc.json` to include the `stm32cube` framework:
```
  "frameworks": [
    "arduino",
    "stm32cube",
    "zephyr"
  ],
```

Clone `STM32CubeWL` from github using the following command: `git clone --recursive https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeWL`, then make sure to add this `package.json`:
```
{
  "description": "STM32Cube is a set of tools and embedded software bricks available free of charge to enable fast and easy development on the STM32 platform (STM32CubeWL MCU Firmware Package)",
  "keywords": [
    "framework",
    "hal",
    "stm32",
    "st"
  ],
  "name": "framework-stm32cubewl",
  "version": "1.26.2",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeWL"
}
```

Then, remove the `.git` subdirectory to prevent compatibility when using our git `buoy-stm32`, since it is a descendant of it.